{"created": "2022-06-12T04:40:32.614952+00:00", "modified": "2022-06-14T10:15:09.291020+00:00", "id": 6624726, "conceptrecid": "6517397", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.6624726", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.6517397", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6624726", "metadata": {"title": "The PI-CAI Challenge: Public Training and Development Dataset", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.6624726", "publication_date": "2022-06-10", "description": "<p>This dataset represents the <strong><a href=\"https://pi-cai.grand-challenge.org/\">PI-CAI</a>: Public Training and Development Dataset</strong>.&nbsp;It contains 1500 anonymized prostate biparametric MRI scans from 1476 patients, acquired between 2012-2021, at three centers (Radboud University Medical Center, University Medical Center Groningen, Ziekenhuis Groep Twente) based in The Netherlands.</p>\n\n<p>The PI-CAI challenge is an all-new grand challenge that aims to validate the diagnostic performance of artificial intelligence and radiologists at clinically significant prostate cancer (csPCa) detection/diagnosis in MRI, with histopathology and follow-up (&ge; 3 years) as the reference standard, in a retrospective setting. The study hypothesizes that state-of-the-art AI algorithms, trained using thousands of patient exams, are non-inferior to radiologists reading bpMRI.</p>\n\n<p>Key aspects of the PI-CAI study design have been established in conjunction with an international scientific advisory board of 16 experts in prostate AI, radiology and urology &mdash;to unify and standardize present-day guidelines, and to ensure meaningful validation of prostate AI towards clinical translation (<strong><a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2405456921001607\">Reinke et al., 2021</a></strong>).</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Saha, Anindo", "affiliation": "Department of Medical Imaging, Radboud University Medical Center, The Netherlands", "orcid": "0000-0002-5091-9862"}, {"name": "Twilt, Jasper Jonathan", "affiliation": "Department of Medical Imaging, Radboud University Medical Center, The Netherlands", "orcid": "0000-0002-9673-6770"}, {"name": "Bosma, Joeran Sander", "affiliation": "Department of Medical Imaging, Radboud University Medical Center, The Netherlands", "orcid": "0000-0002-6315-124X"}, {"name": "van Ginneken, Bram", "affiliation": "Department of Medical Imaging, Radboud University Medical Center, The Netherlands", "orcid": "0000-0003-2028-8972"}, {"name": "Yakar, Derya", "affiliation": "Department of Radiology, Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging, University Medical Center Groningen, The Netherlands", "orcid": "0000-0002-4920-9441"}, {"name": "Elschot, Mattijs", "affiliation": "Department of Circulation and Medical Imaging, Norwegian University of Science and Technology, Norway", "orcid": "0000-0002-8056-9103"}, {"name": "Veltman, Jeroen", "affiliation": "Department of Radiology, Ziekenhuis Groep Twente, The Netherlands", "orcid": "0000-0002-6824-3987"}, {"name": "F\u00fctterer, Jurgen", "affiliation": "Department of Medical Imaging, Radboud University Medical Center, The Netherlands"}, {"name": "de Rooij, Maarten", "affiliation": "Department of Medical Imaging, Radboud University Medical Center, The Netherlands", "orcid": "0000-0001-7257-7907"}, {"name": "Huisman, Henkjan", "affiliation": "Department of Medical Imaging, Radboud University Medical Center, The Netherlands", "orcid": "0000-0001-6753-3221"}], "keywords": ["prostate cancer", "artificial intelligence", "magnetic resonance imaging", "radiologists", "computer-aided detection and diagnosis"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.6522364", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "resource_type": "publication-report", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "v2.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-nc-4.0"}, "grants": [{"code": "952159", "internal_id": "10.13039/501100000780::952159", "funder": {"name": "European Commission", "doi": "10.13039/501100000780", "acronym": "EC"}, "title": "An AI Platform integrating imaging data and models, supporting precision care through prostate cancer\u2019s continuum", "acronym": "ProCAncer-I", "program": "H2020-EU.3.1.", "url": "https://cordis.europa.eu/projects/952159"}], "communities": [{"id": "grand-challenge"}, {"id": "eu"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "6517397"}}]}}, "title": "The PI-CAI Challenge: Public Training and Development Dataset", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6624726", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6624726", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6624726?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6624726", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6624726", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.6624726", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6624726/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6517397", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6517397", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6517397", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.6517397", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:6624726/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:6624726/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6624726/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6624726/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6624726/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/6624726/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6624726/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6624726/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6624726/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6624726/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6624726/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/6624726/access/